<Item XName="ReadMe" UserName="ReadMe" Type="Notes">
<Description>Example text with pretty printing</Description>
<LibName>Eagleware</LibName>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Phased Array Sys-Parameter&amp;nbsp;Workspace&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;ABSTRACT&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;example shows&amp;nbsp;how&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;frequency dependent RF models affect the phase array performance in the Phased Array Analysis and the RF Link in DataFlow.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;SETUP&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;A 8x8 Tx array was created with the final amplifier using and ADI ADL55541 amplifier. Variables were created for the input power, frequency, and element selection. The simulation data was post processed in equation block &apos;ProcessTxData&apos; to extract the Gain and Power Out for a selected element.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;ANALYSIS&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;Phased Array Data&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;- This table contains the Gain and Power Out for the selected phased array element&amp;nbsp;path for the Phased Array Analysis in folder &apos;1 Sys-Parameter Tx&apos;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;RF Link Power&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;- This graph shows the difference in input and output power in the RF Link for the DataFlow analysis in folder &apos;2 RFLink Sys-Parameter Tx&apos;. The results on this graphs shows the same results as the Phased array analsysis.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;Run equations &apos;PlotPattern2&apos; and &apos;PlotPattern3&apos; to show how the RF design controls the beam direction for &apos;PlotPattern2&apos; and that DataFlow controls the beam direction for &apos;PlotPattern3&apos;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;EXERCISES&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;Change the geometry of the of the array to be based on distance instead of wavelength and notice the beam squint on frequency changes.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
